The root cause of the bug is the incorrect assumption made by the compiler regarding the size limits of the `memcpy()` operation due to the use of `array_size()`. This led to a warning about potential overflow when the size of the data being copied exceeded the actual allocated size, which could result in memory corruption or undefined behavior. The absence of a proper range check allowed for the possibility of `ae_cnt` exceeding the predefined limit, triggering the overflow warning.

